Just a reminder to all that the `stics_budget_comp()` function is very useful for comparing the water and nitrogen budgets of Hi-sAFe vs STICS.

Unfortunately, I did not do a great job documenting `stics_budget_comp()` in hisafer. Basically, it (1) uses `hisafe_budget()` to extract the relevant variables from a hop object and (2) extracts the STICS data from the .bil file that Hi-sAFe can export for a simulation (this requires sticsReport = 1 to be used when defining a simulation). The function the makes many small modifications to units, signs, etc to wrangle the two budgets together and then creates a table comparing the two.

