Time series collected with the Clipick tool contain only an average daily air humidity RHmean

HisAFe requires two daily values of air humidity : the minimum and maximum (RHmin and RHmax).

We suggest here a simple algorithm to generate these two values. Field data show that usually RHmax>95%. If we assume that for non rainy days RHmax=95% and for rainy days RHmax=100%, we can compute RHmin easily : RHmin= 2* RHmean-RHmax

We could improve this simple algorithm by studying actual data for the site if available, and finding a regression prediction of RHmax based on available data (Air min and max temperatures, radiation, wind velocity, rainfall). RHmax is then computed by applying this equation to IPCC data. Then RHmin is computed with the same simple equation

